demux: publish the DTS profile of every audio track at load

codec-profile on the track list was decoder-supplied, so a client learned
it only for the selected track, and only after its decoder opened. DTS
carries its extensions (XLL, XBR, LBR) in the bitstream rather than in
CodecPrivate, so a DTS-HD MA track and the lossy DTS core muxed beside it
both read "dts" until then, and a track picker cannot tell them apart
(plezy#2603).

demux_mkv runs libavcodec's DTS parser, the one ad_spdif already uses to
probe passthrough, over the first block of each DTS track, found in the
same bounded block queue probe_x264_garbage() reads. demux_lavf publishes
the profile its stream probing already parsed into codecpar for audio
streams (MPEG-TS and the other formats it probes). The decoder still
replaces either with its own answer once it runs.

diff --git a/demux/demux_lavf.c b/demux/demux_lavf.c
